1.16.m:
Reside there constantly, having enjoyed
pleasures unattainable even by the gods;
meditate upon me continually through the discipline of devotion;
at the burning of the cosmic cycle you shall enter into me again.”

This valor of the dwarf has been recounted to you, O brahmins;
that Supreme Spirit always accomplishes the tasks of the gods.

Thus ends the sixteenth chapter in the former section of the compilation of six thousand verses in the glorious Kūrma Purāṇa.

1.23.m:
From him came Svayaṃbhoja; from him Hṛdika, the tormentor of foes;
then his son was Kṛtavarman; Devara is remembered as his son;
that wise Śūra was his son, and Vasudeva was his son.
